# Sourcing Company Diversification Walkthrough

We implemented client-side company diversity filtering to prevent candidate pool domination by any single employer, optimizing credit spend by filtering candidates prior to profile enrichment.

## Summary of Changes

### 1. Sourcing Over-fetching
- **[apollo_service.py](file:///e:/hiring-agent-v2/backend/services/apollo_service.py)**: Raised Apollo API single-page request limit (`per_page`) up to 100 results, allowing the agent to request the complete overfetched pool in a single API roundtrip.
- **[hiring_graph.py](file:///e:/hiring-agent-v2/backend/agents/hiring_graph.py)**: Configured the `node_apollo_search` sourcing node to calculate and request an overfetch size equal to `min(target_count * 3, 100)`.

### 2. Diversification Utility
- **[diversifier.py](file:///e:/hiring-agent-v2/backend/utils/diversifier.py)**: Created a generic, reusable client-side deduplication utility `diversify_by_company` that limits per-employer representation to a target threshold.

### 3. Normalizer & Sourcing Graph Piping
- **[candidate_normalizer.py](file:///e:/hiring-agent-v2/backend/services/candidate_normalizer.py)**: Improved `clean_company` regex logic to standardize corporate suffixes (Inc, Corp, Co) optionally without dots, which drastically improves company matching.
- **[hiring_graph.py](file:///e:/hiring-agent-v2/backend/agents/hiring_graph.py)**: Wired `diversify_by_company` directly at the end of the `node_candidate_normalizer` step (which operates on cleaned company names). This runs strictly **before** `node_apollo_enrichment`, meaning the paid email/phone reveal credits are ONLY spent on the final, diversified pool (up to `target_count`), not the full overfetched list.

